Patient Name: Maria Lopez
DOB: 1972-09-03
MRN: 87654321
Admission Date: 2026-05-10
Discharge Date: 2026-05-15
Primary Diagnosis: Acute ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI)
Hospital Course Summary:
- Presented with chest pain; underwent emergent coronary angiography with PCI to the LAD with stent placement.
- Hemodynamically stable post-procedure; troponin peaked at 48 ng/mL and trended down.
- Started on dual antiplatelet therapy and high-intensity statin.
Medications at Discharge:
- Aspirin 81 mg PO daily
- Clopidogrel 75 mg PO daily
- Atorvastatin 80 mg PO nightly
- Metoprolol tartrate 25 mg PO twice daily
- Nitroglycerin 0.4 mg SL PRN chest pain
Follow-up:
- Cardiology clinic in 1 week; cardiac rehabilitation referral.
- Primary care in 1-2 weeks for risk-factor management.
Home Instructions:
- Avoid heavy lifting or vigorous exercise until cleared by cardiology.
- If chest pain returns, take one dose of nitroglycerin and call emergency services if pain persists.
Return Precautions / Red Flags:
- New or worsening chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting, or sudden weakness -> seek emergency care.
Allergies: Penicillin (rash)
Discharge Disposition: Home with outpatient cardiac rehab
